speechtext:
But if they do it the control lies in section 13. Section 13 goes on to say;
In the event of the company at any time creating hydraulic or electrical power,
That section brings them under the control of the Board of Railway Commissioners for Canada, and it does not provide for the sale and distribution of electrical power at all. It does not give the company power to sell or distribute it to any municipality or over a transmission line or do any of the things which my hon. friend imagines the Bill enables them to do in order to bolster up some other theory. There is no other purpose behind this Bill than the purpose of building a canal.
